@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: Future after MVP. Provider, advanced Sprint/review, or untrusted execution requirement retained as deferred.
skinparam backgroundColor #0D1525
skinparam defaultFontColor #EDF4FF
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 5
skinparam ArrowColor #91AED1
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #17405A
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #91AED1
skinparam sequenceActorBorderColor #91AED1
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #91AED1
skinparam sequenceGroupBackgroundColor #1A2940
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #91AED1
skinparam sequenceDividerBackgroundColor #1A2940
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #4A302B
skinparam noteBorderColor #F1AD8A
skinparam maxMessageSize 220
hide footbox
autonumber
title AFTER MVP — SB-M14 — Target-authorized deployment is a separate goal
actor "Deployment requester" as U
participant "Deployment authorization" as A
participant "Run output / revision context" as O
participant "Intended target (external boundary)" as T
U -> A : Request exact artifact / revision for intended target
A -> O : Evaluate intended provenance and availability
O --> A : Actual identified context or mismatch / unavailable
A -> A : Check separate target authority / approval / readiness
alt Missing approval, mismatch or ineligible conditions
 A --> U : Denied / blocked; no target action
else Separately eligible target action
 A -> T : Perform only approved intended action
 alt Target effect confirmed
  T --> A : Actual bounded completion evidence
  A --> U : Confirmed intended deployment outcome
 else Definite failed result
  T --> A : Actual failure / partial effects
  A --> U : Failed / partial; recovery follows reviewed policy
 else Effect or response uncertain
  A --> U : Unknown; reconcile target before retry
 end
end
note over A,T
Push, merge, checks and run success cannot approve the target.
No universal rollback or safe replay is assumed.
end note
legend bottom
Logical domain interaction, not runtime execution evidence.
Detailed proposed guards/policies retain their primary status.
endlegend
@enduml
